      "writtenOn": "2017-05-03T01:54:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From my perspective, the correct fix is to have the RIL pass up an int32, correctly switching from 0xFF to the standard \"unset\" value of 0x7FFFFFFF that\u0027s used elsewhere.\n\nActually, I did a little digging and found this:\nhttps://b.corp.google.com/issues/28299027\n\nhttps://googleplex-android-review.git.corp.google.com/#/c/1008533/\n\nThis was a quick patch that was never intended to last, and at that time I suggested converting to uint32_t. :-) Regardless of where a hack lives, it\u0027s still a hack.",
      "parentUuid": "9619413f_a7072603",
      "revId": "b808a31b9b0b5104b4ff32860c7ff9d52c12a7c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
